---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "How do we determine the correct screen dimensions and pixel pitch?",
    answer: "Pixel pitch is determined strictly by minimum viewing distance: each millimetre of pitch corresponds to approximately one metre of viewing distance (e.g. a P3 display is crisp from 3 metres). Sizing depends on gatehouse boom geometry or atrium height. During our on-site survey, we calculate exact sightlines and approach speeds so you never overpay for unneeded pixel density."
  },
  {
    question: "Does the outdoor display comply with municipal outdoor advertising by-laws?",
    answer: "Yes. South African municipal frameworks (including Cape Town, Johannesburg, and George Municipality) distinguish between on-premises estate communications and third-party commercial advertising. Our outdoor displays feature calibrated ambient lux sensors that automatically dim output below municipal caps (such as 1,000 cd/m²) at dusk, complying with local dark-sky regulations."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the installation satisfy Body Corporate PMR 29 and HOA procedures?",
    answer: "Under the Sectional Titles Schemes Management Act 8 of 2011, displays are classified as common-property improvements. By dedicating the screen to essential community utility—security alerts, municipal outage notices, and AGM reminders—the installation qualifies under Prescribed Management Rule 29(2) as a 'reasonably necessary' improvement requiring a 30-day notice rather than a unanimous vote. We furnish itemised engineering proposals suitable for trustee sign-off."
  },
  {
    question: "Who manages the structural steelwork, wind loading, and electrical compliance?",
    answer: "We provide complete turnkey installation accountability. Our technicians manage custom structural steel brackets engineered to SANS 10160 wind-load standards, concealed cabling, dedicated sub-distribution breakers, and certified electrical compliance under SANS 10142-1 (issuing an electrical CoC upon handover)."
  },
  {
    question: "How complex is daily content scheduling for non-technical office staff?",
    answer: "No dedicated IT personnel or graphic design skills are required. The cloud CMS runs in any desktop or mobile browser. Estate managers or marketing staff can select pre-formatted notice templates, schedule automated dayparted playlists, and publish announcements in under 90 seconds. We include 1-on-1 operator training upon handover."
  },
  {
    question: "Can our property use optional advertising slots to offset capital costs?",
    answer: "Yes, where approved by trustees or commercial asset managers. For shopping centres and mixed-use precincts, commercial advertising slots generate recurring non-GLA revenue. For residential estates, trustees frequently approve vetted local community service sponsors (security providers, schools, golf clubs) to subsidise CapEx without visual clutter."
  }
];
---

<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="faq-header">
      <span class="section-index">07 / GOVERNANCE & FAQ</span>
      <h2 id="faq-heading" class="section-title">
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>
    </div>

    <!-- Flush-Left Hairline Accordion List -->
    <div class="minimal-faq-list" role="region" aria-label="Frequently Asked Questions">
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="minimal-faq-item">
          <summary class="minimal-faq-summary">
            <span class="faq-question-text">{faq.question}</span>
            <span class="faq-icon-indicator" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="icon-plus">+</span>
              <span class="icon-minus">−</span>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="minimal-faq-body">
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-header {
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .minimal-faq-list {
    max-width: 900px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-hairline);
  }

  .minimal-faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-hairline);
  }

  .minimal-faq-summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding-block: 1.5rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
    list-style: none;
    min-height: 44px;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .minimal-faq-summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-question-text {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .minimal-faq-summary:hover .faq-question-text {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .faq-icon-indicator {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .icon-minus {
    display: none;
  }

  .minimal-faq-item[open] .icon-plus {
    display: none;
  }

  .minimal-faq-item[open] .icon-minus {
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .minimal-faq-body {
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
</style>
